A||N||5||fierose||Fiero with 239,000 miles||||1||
Z||000000||fierose||10-07-2001||09:34 PM||||Just was wondering what the opinion was on a car with this many miles on the body. The car has been maintained very well but the suspension i.e. the bushings everywhere seem to be shot.  It's got a new tranny and engine.  I'm just asking if there is a point to where I should get one with fewer miles or go through the work to fix it up.  I just don't want to work on restoring it and find out it's not worth it.  Any advice on things to look out for suspension/steering wise would be great.<P>Thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-07-2001||09:52 PM||||I only had about $6000 to spend on my car. I couldn't find one with low miles AND the Getrag 5spd. They were usually creampuffs that had an auto. Usually in the $7500-$8500 range. <P>I lucked out with my 88GT. It is high mileage as far as 1980 ere american cars go with 102K, but that isn't a lot of mileage when you consider the age. It needed a serious tuneup in the worst way, but it is running better and better. I'm thrilled with it.<P>As to the Fiero you are looking at, if you are mechanically inclined you can change all the bushings and tighten up the suspension inexpensively. I'm gonna have all that looked at when I buy a set of Eibach lowering springs here soon. The idiot original owner heated the front springs on mine a little as you can see by the pic. I like the look, but not the ride.<BR>You have a motor and tranny too! Whatever Fiero you find will be all the better for it. Good luck in your hunt!<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||10-07-2001||10:33 PM||||price? model? if its worth restoring and the price is right go for it. if i were you, i'd be patient! i looked for a month before i found my car, 87 gt, fully loaded, 95k miles, lots of new parts, 30k mile getrag, for 1200!!!! just wait, good deals will come<P>------------------<BR>87 fiero gt under semi restoration/modification. progress at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-07-2001||11:11 PM||||I'd be most concerned with the condition of the spaceframe, ie. Rust or evidence of accident damage.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||10-08-2001||01:10 AM||||I agree with Tigger,  if the spaceframe is ok, then the suspension stuff is cheap and even pretty easy to do for a hobby mechanic.  I have done complete suspension and engine rebuilds on two V6 Fieros and will be starting on the third in a month or two with my 15 year old son.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-08-2001||09:14 AM||||The 88 that I have has 180,000 on it and was not taken very good care of before I got it. But, there was no frame damage or rust so I just started throwing new stuff on it. The biggest help was the new shocks/struts and suspension bushings. Try not to give too much for the initial investment because all the little things to buy add up in a hurry (engine swaps, leather seats, big brakes, supercharger, new paint. . . )||||reg||1
